1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,100
<i>Joey saw it in Major Aglipay's
belongings.</i>

2
00:00:03,233 --> 00:00:04,100
<i> That's it.</i>

3
00:00:04,233 --> 00:00:05,667
<i>That's the video
that will free Father!</i>

4
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:08,467
<i>Could this be what your Korean
friend was talking about?</i>

5
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:09,900
<i> It's Theresa.</i>

6
00:00:10,033 --> 00:00:11,433
<i>Bro, what happened?
Did you catch Theresa?</i>

7
00:00:11,567 --> 00:00:13,133
<i> Not yet, but I know I'm close.</i>

8
00:00:13,267 --> 00:00:14,400
<i> Me too, I have good news too.</i>

9
00:00:14,533 --> 00:00:17,500
<i>The broken flash drive,
there's a copy.</i>

10
00:00:17,633 --> 00:00:18,600
<i> Where is it?</i>

11
00:00:18,733 --> 00:00:20,600
<i>Joey sent it to the attorney
for evidence.</i>

12
00:00:20,733 --> 00:00:23,000
<i>Just a little bit, Father,
you can go home.</i>

13
00:00:23,133 --> 00:00:25,100
<i> We'll be together again.</i>

14
00:00:25,233 --> 00:00:28,333
<i>I heard you need help
with your husband's case.</i>

15
00:00:28,467 --> 00:00:29,833
<i>I don't want to bother you
anymore.</i>

16
00:00:29,967 --> 00:00:32,267
<i>There's new evidence
that just came out.</i>

17
00:00:32,400 --> 00:00:34,733
<i> Delgado got new evidence.</i>

18
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:36,200
<i>Find out what it is right away.</i>

19
00:00:36,333 --> 00:00:37,800
<i> I need to see Berdugo.</i>

20
00:00:37,933 --> 00:00:40,033
<i>He's meeting with his new
partners</i>

21
00:00:40,167 --> 00:00:40,733
<i> at the end of the month.</i>

22
00:00:40,867 --> 00:00:41,800
<i> The video evidence,</i>

23
00:00:41,933 --> 00:00:43,200
<i>are you going to release it
to the public?</i>

24
00:00:43,333 --> 00:00:43,733
<i> Yeah.</i>

25
00:00:43,867 --> 00:00:44,600
<i> Which means...</i>

26
00:00:44,733 --> 00:00:45,867
<i> she will be a wanted woman.</i>

27
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:47,133
<i>I know you what you want
to happen,</i>

28
00:00:47,267 --> 00:00:49,767
<i>but I can't ignore
the new evidence.</i>

29
00:00:49,900 --> 00:00:51,967
<i>Because of the evidence
that came out</i>

30
00:00:52,100 --> 00:00:53,933
<i>in the case of Major
Miguel Delgado,</i>

31
00:00:54,067 --> 00:00:56,467
<i>the Court has made a decision,
Ka-Tiradas.</i>

32
00:00:56,600 --> 00:00:59,633
<i>The former police officer
has been proven innocent.</i>

33
00:00:59,767 --> 00:01:01,967
<i>It's better for me to leave now</i>

34
00:01:02,100 --> 00:01:05,633
<i> because the movements of
Berdugo's group are restricted.</i>

35
00:01:05,767 --> 00:01:08,133
<i>Golda, thank you very much
for your help.</i>

36
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:10,067
<i>You fixed my mother and father's
relationship.</i>

37
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:12,967
<i>And even though your statement
was rejected,</i>

38
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:15,300
<i>I'm still grateful
that you did it.</i>

39
00:01:33,333 --> 00:01:36,200
Why are you still there?
Leave now.

40
00:01:36,333 --> 00:01:37,933
We're getting ready, Boss.

41
00:01:38,067 --> 00:01:39,133
<i> Leave now</i>

42
00:01:39,267 --> 00:01:42,267
and don't come back while
the situation is still hot.

43
00:01:42,433 --> 00:01:44,867
<i>I don't want our operations
to be jeopardized</i>

44
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,733
just because of you two.

45
00:01:46,867 --> 00:01:48,733
<i> No one knows we're here.</i>

46
00:01:48,867 --> 00:01:50,867
Maybe I can just hide here.

47
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,400
<i> I thought you were smart?</i>

48
00:01:52,533 --> 00:01:56,000
Do you think no one else
will see you there?

49
00:01:56,133 --> 00:01:59,433
<i>Leave now if you don't want me
to force you out.</i>

50
00:01:59,567 --> 00:02:00,900
Leave now!

51
00:02:14,567 --> 00:02:16,200
Thanks to you guys,

52
00:02:17,233 --> 00:02:19,600
because of you, Father is free.

53
00:02:21,667 --> 00:02:22,833
We won.

54
00:02:24,833 --> 00:02:27,667
You, of all people,
you know you're close to me.

55
00:02:30,267 --> 00:02:31,333
Come on.

56
00:02:37,867 --> 00:02:40,433
Sir Oppa, thank you so much.

57
00:02:40,567 --> 00:02:41,800
You're welcome.

58
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:50,867
Andrew, thank you.

59
00:02:51,900 --> 00:02:53,067
Boss Budol.

60
00:02:54,633 --> 00:02:55,767
Welcome.

61
00:03:06,533 --> 00:03:07,567
I have to go.

62
00:03:08,767 --> 00:03:11,867
You know, I'm working on a new
lead where I can find Theresa.

63
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:14,933
I'm hoping that it pays off
this time.

64
00:03:15,067 --> 00:03:16,600
Okay, you be safe.

65
00:03:16,733 --> 00:03:18,533
Also, once you catch Theresa,

66
00:03:18,667 --> 00:03:21,267
you ask all of them who their
mastermind is.

67
00:03:21,433 --> 00:03:23,033
Gotta put all of them in jail.

68
00:03:23,167 --> 00:03:24,167
Yes.

69
00:03:45,467 --> 00:03:46,567
Why are you following me?

70
00:03:46,700 --> 00:03:47,800
I'm going with you.

71
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:48,833
Let's go.

72
00:03:51,000 --> 00:03:52,933
You know what the problem is?

73
00:03:55,033 --> 00:03:56,200
What?

74
00:03:56,333 --> 00:04:00,167
You give up too easily instead
of chasing what you want.

75
00:04:01,233 --> 00:04:02,967
- No, I don't.
- No, you did!

76
00:04:03,100 --> 00:04:08,633
You just left the house because
you've given up on Joey.

77
00:04:10,200 --> 00:04:12,033
Well, she doesn't like me.

78
00:04:12,167 --> 00:04:13,200
She likes someone else.

79
00:04:13,333 --> 00:04:14,567
Did she say that?

80
00:04:18,367 --> 00:04:18,933
See?

81
00:04:19,067 --> 00:04:20,400
Then why not?

82
00:04:20,533 --> 00:04:23,567
You will never know
unless you ask.

83
00:04:24,833 --> 00:04:27,267
Is that how you make the moves
with the girls?

84
00:04:27,400 --> 00:04:29,067
You just push, push, push?

85
00:04:31,767 --> 00:04:33,233
If you're asking...

86
00:04:36,867 --> 00:04:39,033
if I go after what I want,

87
00:04:40,067 --> 00:04:41,567
then yes.

88
00:04:41,700 --> 00:04:45,000
I will not stop
until she's mine.

89
00:04:54,467 --> 00:04:55,533
Come in.

90
00:04:57,900 --> 00:04:59,033
Peter.

91
00:05:01,433 --> 00:05:05,267
I was going to talk to you two.

92
00:05:07,467 --> 00:05:08,933
What?

93
00:05:09,067 --> 00:05:10,267
Why?

94
00:05:15,733 --> 00:05:19,700
Maybe this is the last time
we'll be together.

95
00:05:22,067 --> 00:05:23,000
Why?

96
00:05:25,267 --> 00:05:27,433
I'm going home.

97
00:05:27,567 --> 00:05:29,733
I want to be with my family.

98
00:05:33,233 --> 00:05:35,700
I understand.

99
00:05:35,867 --> 00:05:40,833
Of course, you've been dreaming
of that for a long time,

100
00:05:40,967 --> 00:05:42,033
haven't you?

101
00:05:43,733 --> 00:05:48,100
Just call if you need anything.
I'll be right there.

102
00:05:49,967 --> 00:05:51,200
Same here.

103
00:05:54,167 --> 00:05:56,067
Thank you to both of you.

104
00:05:57,400 --> 00:05:59,367
How's that?

105
00:05:59,500 --> 00:06:02,100
Our lives are back to normal.

106
00:06:03,400 --> 00:06:08,467
So, you are going back
to Tirada Express as Boss Idol.

107
00:06:08,633 --> 00:06:12,767
And you, of course, will work.

108
00:06:12,900 --> 00:06:17,633
Then, Jin Ho,
his search will continue,

109
00:06:17,767 --> 00:06:20,533
and he will definitely catch
that Theresa.

110
00:06:34,433 --> 00:06:37,833
I'll just call you when
it's not too hot and safe.

111
00:06:44,067 --> 00:06:45,600
Okay.

112
00:06:45,733 --> 00:06:47,633
Don't be pissed off.

113
00:06:47,767 --> 00:06:51,367
Just be grateful,
he's just asking you to hide.

114
00:06:51,500 --> 00:06:53,567
We know what can happen.

115
00:06:53,700 --> 00:06:55,567
I'm a little hesitant

116
00:06:55,700 --> 00:06:59,267
about Jin Ho searching
for Theresa Park

117
00:07:00,433 --> 00:07:03,500
because he doesn't want
to cooperate with the police.

118
00:07:03,633 --> 00:07:05,567
There's nothing wrong with that.

119
00:07:05,700 --> 00:07:08,533
Of course, he might want to get
Theresa on his own.

120
00:07:15,433 --> 00:07:17,267
But the thing is, he's Interpol,

121
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:20,300
and he has to cooperate
with the police.

122
00:07:21,533 --> 00:07:23,133
You know, I feel like...

123
00:07:24,367 --> 00:07:26,233
there's something personal
going on

124
00:07:26,367 --> 00:07:28,167
in his search for Theresa.

125
00:07:28,300 --> 00:07:31,500
I wouldn't be like a mouse
hiding from a cat

126
00:07:31,633 --> 00:07:34,100
if it weren't for the person
who took the video.

127
00:07:34,233 --> 00:07:35,667
I want my revenge.

128
00:07:36,833 --> 00:07:38,133
That's going to happen.

129
00:07:38,267 --> 00:07:41,267
We'll find her and make her pay.

130
00:07:41,400 --> 00:07:43,700
That's exactly what I'm going
to do.

131
00:07:43,833 --> 00:07:47,067
I'll even take a video of her
while I'm killing her.

132
00:07:47,200 --> 00:07:49,467
Call it poetic justice.

133
00:08:15,733 --> 00:08:18,700
Well, maybe that's what happens
when you're in law enforcement.

134
00:08:18,833 --> 00:08:20,367
Just like what happened
to Father.

135
00:08:20,500 --> 00:08:21,900
That's personal.

136
00:08:23,267 --> 00:08:27,267
Oh well, I'm sure that
when Jin Ho catches Theresa,

137
00:08:27,400 --> 00:08:29,733
he'll also find out
where her accomplices are,

138
00:08:29,867 --> 00:08:32,667
and then everyone in the
syndicate will be caught.

139
00:08:32,800 --> 00:08:34,933
Our lives will be peaceful.

140
00:08:46,067 --> 00:08:47,200
Who's that?

141
00:08:48,467 --> 00:08:49,767
Hurry up!

142
00:08:51,267 --> 00:08:52,667
Hurry up!

143
00:09:15,067 --> 00:09:16,367
Get out of the car.

144
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:18,933
Get out!

145
00:09:34,967 --> 00:09:36,933
Joey, I'll just check
our booking.

146
00:09:37,067 --> 00:09:38,700
I'll just go there.
I'll just wait for you.

147
00:09:43,367 --> 00:09:44,533
Andrew,

148
00:09:46,933 --> 00:09:49,667
thanks for all your help?

149
00:09:49,800 --> 00:09:51,800
At least, now your life
will be peaceful

150
00:09:51,933 --> 00:09:52,800
because there won't be
an immature person

151
00:09:52,933 --> 00:09:54,367
bothering you anymore.

152
00:09:56,533 --> 00:09:57,867
Well, about that...

153
00:09:58,967 --> 00:10:01,633
You're so sensitive sometimes.

154
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:05,033
And I get it,

155
00:10:06,867 --> 00:10:08,200
it's really foul,

156
00:10:09,233 --> 00:10:10,700
so I'm sorry.

157
00:10:12,733 --> 00:10:19,500
I'm sorry if I misjudged you
just because you're younger.

158
00:10:22,267 --> 00:10:25,067
I actually think that you're
strong and smart,

159
00:10:26,567 --> 00:10:29,467
and you're determined
in everything you do.

160
00:10:32,700 --> 00:10:33,933
Also,

161
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:39,133
everybody's lucky to have you
by their side.

162
00:10:40,400 --> 00:10:42,000
Wow!

163
00:10:42,133 --> 00:10:44,867
Coming from Boss Budol, really?

164
00:10:46,867 --> 00:10:49,633
I'm just praising you now.

165
00:10:53,500 --> 00:10:59,100
Can we get rid of
that "Boss Budol?"

166
00:10:59,233 --> 00:11:00,467
No.

167
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:04,333
No, but seriously,

168
00:11:04,467 --> 00:11:08,933
thank you very much because
your opinion of me has changed.

169
00:11:09,100 --> 00:11:11,833
I, too, have changed
my opinion of you.

170
00:11:11,967 --> 00:11:14,767
I only knew you because
of three traits.

171
00:11:16,133 --> 00:11:20,867
Irritable, hot-headed,
and moody.

172
00:11:21,933 --> 00:11:24,433
Wow, you're being sorry
with that.

173
00:11:24,567 --> 00:11:27,100
Wait, let me finish.

174
00:11:27,233 --> 00:11:30,933
I'll also say that it
has also changed

175
00:11:31,067 --> 00:11:34,800
because I saw that you care too.

176
00:11:46,767 --> 00:11:48,667
I'm so happy you caught me.

177
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,233
I need you.

178
00:11:56,533 --> 00:11:57,867
I'm in trouble.

179
00:11:58,967 --> 00:12:00,600
I need you, Baby.

180
00:12:17,700 --> 00:12:20,100
But I have some advice for you.

181
00:12:20,233 --> 00:12:25,600
Smile often and have high energy
than normal.

182
00:12:25,733 --> 00:12:27,233
- That's it.
- Like this?

183
00:12:27,367 --> 00:12:28,333
Yes.

184
00:12:30,067 --> 00:12:34,300
Like a celebrity,
outside the salon poster.

185
00:12:34,433 --> 00:12:35,400
Let me see.

186
00:12:36,633 --> 00:12:37,800
That.

187
00:12:40,833 --> 00:12:43,567
- Show me a smile.
- Joey!

188
00:12:43,700 --> 00:12:45,500
- Show me a smile...
- Smile?

189
00:12:45,633 --> 00:12:47,400
Let's go, our ride is ready.

190
00:12:53,267 --> 00:12:56,700
So, see you around, Boss Budol?

191
00:12:59,233 --> 00:13:02,000
See you, JoeyOnDuty.

192
00:13:26,567 --> 00:13:28,800
I'm done falling for your games.

193
00:13:30,533 --> 00:13:31,967
We had a deal.

194
00:13:33,567 --> 00:13:36,700
We were supposed to escape
together, right?

195
00:13:36,833 --> 00:13:38,367
But you...

196
00:13:40,967 --> 00:13:43,300
You left me.

197
00:13:43,433 --> 00:13:44,633
I was scared.

198
00:13:46,300 --> 00:13:47,867
I didn't know who to trust.

199
00:13:49,167 --> 00:13:52,233
I doubted you.

200
00:13:52,367 --> 00:13:53,333
I'm sorry.

201
00:13:54,567 --> 00:13:55,967
But you...

202
00:13:56,100 --> 00:13:58,433
You're the only one
who didn't give up on me.

203
00:13:59,533 --> 00:14:00,933
But you...

204
00:14:01,067 --> 00:14:04,100
you did everything to find me.

205
00:14:04,233 --> 00:14:05,500
Yes.

206
00:14:05,633 --> 00:14:07,667
So I found you now.

207
00:14:07,800 --> 00:14:10,767
To bring you back to Scorpio

208
00:14:10,900 --> 00:14:15,067
so you can be punished
for running away

209
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:17,433
and stealing from us.

210
00:14:20,800 --> 00:14:26,300
And stealing this from me.

211
00:14:29,633 --> 00:14:31,167
Really?

212
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:33,267
Is that really what you want?

213
00:14:34,867 --> 00:14:37,067
To watch me get punished?

214
00:14:37,200 --> 00:14:38,400
Tortured?

215
00:14:40,167 --> 00:14:41,900
Can you really live with that?

216
00:14:44,033 --> 00:14:45,867
I know you still love me.

217
00:14:48,167 --> 00:14:50,100
I know you can't let go of me.

218
00:14:53,467 --> 00:14:55,733
So instead of handing me over
to die,

219
00:14:57,100 --> 00:14:58,267
come with me.

220
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:00,500
You and I,

221
00:15:00,633 --> 00:15:04,200
we fight back against everyone
who wants to bring us apart

222
00:15:04,367 --> 00:15:05,800
and bring us down.

223
00:15:06,867 --> 00:15:09,000
Let's finish what we started
together.

224
00:15:11,267 --> 00:15:12,300
Join me.

225
00:15:13,967 --> 00:15:15,333
Join me, Baby.

226
00:15:16,767 --> 00:15:18,100
Join me.

227
00:15:24,367 --> 00:15:25,267
Mother!

228
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:26,933
Okay.

229
00:15:27,067 --> 00:15:32,000
It's a good thing your
break isn't over yet,

230
00:15:32,367 --> 00:15:34,800
and you'll be with us
for a long time.

231
00:15:34,967 --> 00:15:37,067
You came home right on time.

232
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,833
The bathroom upstairs is dirty.

233
00:15:38,967 --> 00:15:42,433
And the grass here in our
backyard is already tall.

234
00:15:42,567 --> 00:15:43,567
You know what you're going
to do.

235
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:45,300
What are you saying?

236
00:15:45,433 --> 00:15:47,567
I'm not going to order
my daughter around.

237
00:15:47,700 --> 00:15:49,700
We're going to have a QT.

238
00:15:49,833 --> 00:15:51,267
What cutie?

239
00:15:51,400 --> 00:15:52,967
I didn't say you were cute.

240
00:15:53,100 --> 00:15:54,867
What I said was, QT.

241
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,367
Your father went buffering
again.

242
00:15:56,500 --> 00:16:00,567
Do you know why?
He doesn't know what QT means.

243
00:16:00,700 --> 00:16:02,700
What is QT?

244
00:16:02,833 --> 00:16:04,667
Quality time, Father.

245
00:16:04,800 --> 00:16:07,067
Of course,
Mother and I missed you.

246
00:16:07,200 --> 00:16:08,367
Let's have some quality time.

247
00:16:08,533 --> 00:16:11,000
Okay, okay, okay.

248
00:16:11,133 --> 00:16:12,233
Come on, come on, come on.

249
00:16:13,267 --> 00:16:15,133
Wait a minute?
Someone's calling.

250
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:18,333
Peter, why?

251
00:16:18,467 --> 00:16:19,800
Joey, are you home already?

252
00:16:19,933 --> 00:16:21,533
<i> Yes, I just got home.</i>

253
00:16:21,667 --> 00:16:25,600
That's good, but Jin Ho,
do you have any news?

254
00:16:25,733 --> 00:16:27,433
<i>Is he home?
He hasn't replied yet.</i>

255
00:16:27,567 --> 00:16:28,533
Wow.

256
00:16:28,667 --> 00:16:31,200
You're so clingy to your Oppa.

257
00:16:31,333 --> 00:16:32,933
<i> I might get jealous.</i>

258
00:16:34,833 --> 00:16:35,767
Hey, who are you talking to?

259
00:16:35,900 --> 00:16:37,367
What jealousy are you
talking about?

260
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:39,633
It's just Peter.

261
00:16:39,767 --> 00:16:41,200
Peter, Father.

262
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:43,867
Hi, Peter.

263
00:16:44,933 --> 00:16:46,233
Hello, Major.

264
00:16:46,367 --> 00:16:49,333
<i>Thank you so much
for your help with Joey.</i>

265
00:16:49,467 --> 00:16:51,000
I'm free now.

266
00:16:51,133 --> 00:16:53,033
<i> Uncle, that's nothing.</i>

267
00:16:53,167 --> 00:16:55,100
I'm just making up because,
of course,

268
00:16:55,233 --> 00:16:57,367
your daughter is a good person.

269
00:16:57,500 --> 00:17:00,367
<i>And of course,
I can't forsake her either.</i>

270
00:17:00,500 --> 00:17:02,967
Besides, I don't want her hurt.

271
00:17:03,100 --> 00:17:06,500
You know that she's important
to me, so...

272
00:17:07,600 --> 00:17:09,800
You know, you're really an
oversharer.

273
00:17:09,933 --> 00:17:11,333
Father gets it.

274
00:17:11,467 --> 00:17:13,867
<i> Okay, let's talk later.</i>

275
00:17:14,000 --> 00:17:15,967
Don't miss me, okay? Bye.

276
00:17:18,600 --> 00:17:20,000
Come on. Sit down, sit down.

277
00:17:20,133 --> 00:17:22,933
- Yes, I'm hungry. Let's go.
- Come on.

278
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,800
They even mentioned
missing each other.

279
00:17:28,133 --> 00:17:29,800
Let's pray first.

280
00:17:31,100 --> 00:17:33,067
Lord, thank you for today.

281
00:17:33,200 --> 00:17:36,167
Thank you again
because we're together.

282
00:17:36,300 --> 00:17:39,033
Thank you for the food
in front of us today.

283
00:17:39,167 --> 00:17:39,767
Amen.

284
00:17:39,900 --> 00:17:41,400
Amen.

285
00:17:51,900 --> 00:17:53,500
Okay, how about this...

286
00:17:53,633 --> 00:17:55,800
Godfather and the fallen deal.

287
00:17:57,000 --> 00:17:58,833
It's still fresh and a big name.

288
00:17:58,967 --> 00:18:01,633
That's possible.

289
00:18:01,767 --> 00:18:04,000
Hey, that's for the anniversary
expose.

290
00:18:04,133 --> 00:18:06,800
- Right.
- For sure, it'll be trending.

291
00:18:06,933 --> 00:18:08,367
Andrew, what do you think?

292
00:18:10,300 --> 00:18:11,033
Here he is.

293
00:18:11,167 --> 00:18:14,633
- Hello?
- Boss?

294
00:18:14,767 --> 00:18:16,633
What's this, Boss Andrew?

295
00:18:16,767 --> 00:18:19,567
It seems like he doesn't want
to be with us.

296
00:18:19,700 --> 00:18:21,833
He probably wants to be
with his other team.

297
00:18:24,200 --> 00:18:25,533
What are you saying?

298
00:18:27,867 --> 00:18:29,467
I thought of something.

299
00:18:30,633 --> 00:18:36,233
Why don't we interview
Major Miguel Delgado?

300
00:18:36,367 --> 00:18:40,367
Andrew, we're an exposé show.
We're not Tito Boy.

301
00:18:42,567 --> 00:18:47,333
Or maybe he just wants
to see Joey again?

302
00:18:47,467 --> 00:18:48,733
Right?

303
00:18:49,833 --> 00:18:53,267
Didn't it cross your mind
that that's okay?

304
00:18:53,400 --> 00:18:57,100
We'll have a new segment,
a new angle.

305
00:18:57,267 --> 00:19:00,033
So that the people involved
can have a voice, too.

306
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:04,767
Possible.

307
00:19:04,900 --> 00:19:06,100
Good.

308
00:19:06,233 --> 00:19:08,967
There's a human angle.

309
00:19:09,100 --> 00:19:13,267
It seems like there's
an emotional connection.

310
00:19:13,400 --> 00:19:14,533
- Right!
- Right?

311
00:19:14,667 --> 00:19:16,833
That's it, isn't it?
Kyle, come on, make a list.

312
00:19:16,967 --> 00:19:20,267
Let's make a list of names
that we can interview.

313
00:19:20,400 --> 00:19:22,167
Donald Trump!

314
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:24,433
- Hey! Okay!
- That's it!

315
00:19:24,567 --> 00:19:26,033
- Who else?
- Kanye West.

316
00:19:26,167 --> 00:19:27,833
- Awesome, awesome, yeah.
- Okay?

317
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,900
Who else? One more.
Think of someone else?

318
00:19:30,033 --> 00:19:31,467
Okay.

319
00:19:31,600 --> 00:19:33,533
I know who he wants
to interview.

320
00:19:33,667 --> 00:19:34,600
Joey.

321
00:19:44,533 --> 00:19:47,200
Is that the Korean guy,
your crush?

322
00:19:49,033 --> 00:19:53,533
I don't have a crush on him.
Jin Ho is just really funny.

323
00:19:53,667 --> 00:19:55,400
Father.

324
00:19:57,667 --> 00:20:00,767
Well, it's good that you
don't have a crush.

325
00:20:00,900 --> 00:20:02,933
Poor Peter.

326
00:20:03,100 --> 00:20:05,400
Mother, you too.

327
00:20:05,533 --> 00:20:06,533
You're something else.

328
00:20:06,667 --> 00:20:10,000
And Mother,
Peter is just my friend.

329
00:20:10,133 --> 00:20:11,800
Buddy, best friend!

330
00:20:11,933 --> 00:20:13,900
We're just like siblings.

331
00:20:14,033 --> 00:20:17,533
What? Best friend?
Like a brother?

332
00:20:17,667 --> 00:20:19,100
I don't think so.

333
00:20:19,233 --> 00:20:21,300
What did he say earlier?

334
00:20:21,433 --> 00:20:23,300
- "She's important to me."
- There you go.

335
00:20:23,433 --> 00:20:25,033
- Is that just best friends?
- Yes.

336
00:20:25,167 --> 00:20:26,900
- You're something else.
- Yes, Tito Boy.

337
00:20:28,533 --> 00:20:31,867
Father became a gossipmonger
when he was released.

338
00:20:33,067 --> 00:20:36,833
No, but Peter is also important
to me.

339
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:38,100
All of them.

340
00:20:38,233 --> 00:20:40,800
Jin Ho and Andrew, too.

341
00:20:40,933 --> 00:20:43,500
Because what we went through
was so hard.

342
00:20:43,633 --> 00:20:46,267
Besides, they really became
my true friends.

343
00:20:48,067 --> 00:20:50,033
You know, Joey, you're lucky.

344
00:20:50,167 --> 00:20:53,800
It's hard to find those
kinds of friends,

345
00:20:53,933 --> 00:20:57,567
the ones who aren't always there
just because they're just happy.

346
00:20:59,100 --> 00:21:00,867
Your mother was right.

347
00:21:01,000 --> 00:21:05,533
Friends like them, you should
take good care of them.

348
00:21:08,033 --> 00:21:13,367
I hope we can be together again
not because of any problem.

349
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:16,700
That's true.

350
00:21:18,900 --> 00:21:20,667
Come on, let's finish that.

351
00:21:20,800 --> 00:21:21,967
Hey, Mother,
let me help you with that.

352
00:21:22,100 --> 00:21:23,733
There are still some glasses.

353
00:21:29,867 --> 00:21:31,200
Okay, okay.

354
00:21:32,500 --> 00:21:34,767
Now that we don't have to worry
about Lisa,

355
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:36,867
let's focus on the real problem.

356
00:21:41,800 --> 00:21:44,233
I can't believe
he's making headlines

357
00:21:44,367 --> 00:21:47,133
instead of rotting underground.

358
00:21:49,033 --> 00:21:53,367
He just got free,
but he'll never escape us.

359
00:21:55,400 --> 00:21:57,700
He'll bother us again.

360
00:21:59,200 --> 00:22:01,633
He can't make us look weak,
Matias,

361
00:22:01,767 --> 00:22:05,967
especially now that our new deal
is in motion.

362
00:22:09,367 --> 00:22:11,233
I'll take care of that, Berdugo.

363
00:22:35,633 --> 00:22:37,100
Miguel, I know you.

364
00:22:37,233 --> 00:22:38,233
You won't be at peace

365
00:22:38,367 --> 00:22:41,333
if you don't catch the syndicate
that's after you.

366
00:22:41,467 --> 00:22:43,933
I'm going back to service.
I'm going to finish this fight.

367
00:22:44,067 --> 00:22:45,500
By the authority vested in me,

368
00:22:45,633 --> 00:22:49,000
I hereby reinstate you to active
service, Major Miguel Delgado.

369
00:22:49,167 --> 00:22:50,233
Where is Joey?

370
00:22:50,367 --> 00:22:52,233
- Do you need anything from her?
- What do you need?

371
00:22:52,367 --> 00:22:53,767
I tried to keep him out
of this mess,

372
00:22:53,900 --> 00:22:54,767
but he wanted this,

373
00:22:54,900 --> 00:22:57,167
and I can't afford a weapon
pointed at us,

374
00:22:57,300 --> 00:22:58,467
even if he's family.

375
00:22:58,600 --> 00:22:59,467
Like what they say,

376
00:22:59,600 --> 00:23:01,333
we're just getting
to the exciting part.

377
00:23:01,467 --> 00:23:02,467
Ready, Berdugo.

378
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:05,433
Have you thought of a way
to expose the syndicate?

379
00:23:05,567 --> 00:23:06,567
You know, Andrew...
